slow down your progression and revise more often. And if you truly feel entirely lost, you will easily find the way again by starting the course over right now from the first lesson, as, for that matter, we will be recommending before long to all our readers. \par \par }{\b\f210 2.}{\f208  And now, let us tackle the only delicate point of Latin conjugation, the formation of the }{\b\f210 future indicative}{\f208  and the }{\b\f210 present subjunctive}{\f208 .}{\b\f210 \par \par }{\f208 Before starting, it\rquote s not a bad thing to know that the subjunctive is used much more in Latin than in modern English, whence it has as good as disappeared. To start with, in a main clause, it replaces the }{\scaps\f208 conditional}{\f208  (e.g.: }{\b\f210 p}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 ssim si v}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 lim}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 I would be able if I wanted}{\f208 ) and sometimes the }{\scaps\f208 imperative}{\f208  (e.g.: a}{\b\f210 beat!}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 let him leave!}{\f208 ) In a subordinate clause, it is found after certain verbs expressing an order, a necessity or other nuances that you will learn from usage.\par The word }{\b\f210 subjunctive}{\b\i\f212  }{\f208 comes from}{\b\i\f212  }{\b\f210 sub}{\i\f211 , under}{\f208  and }{\b\f210 j}{\f208 u}{\b\f210 ngere}{\f208 , }{\b\f210 j}{\f208 u}{\b\f210 ngo}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 is}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 ere}{\f208 , }{\b\f210 j}{\f208 u}{\b\f210 nxi}{\f208 , }{\b\f210 j}{\f208 u}{\b\f210 nctum}{\i\f211 , to join with a yoke}{\f208 . It should cause no surprise to find it in certain }{\i\f211 subordinate}{\f208  clauses.\par For example, just as one says in some forms of English, \ldblquote I demand that he leave\rdblquote  and not \ldblquote I demand that he leaves\rdblquote , one would say in Latin: i}{\b\f210 mpero ut }{\f208 a}{\b\f210 beat}{\f208  and not }{\b\i\f212 i}{\i\f211 mpero ut }{\b\i\f212 a}{\i\f211 bit}{\f208 .\par Finally the subjunctive is used in the }{\scaps\f208 indirect}{\f208  or }{\scaps\f208 re